{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"ssh-server","name":"SSH server","version":"0.3.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":["exec"],"author":"bertrandom","description":"A real SSH-2 server in pure JS (no binary): interactive ssh is a root line-shell, ssh root@tv 'cmd' runs as root, plus scp/sftp. Needs Node 10+.","main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"SSH server"}},"files":{"README.md":"# SSH server\n\nA real SSH-2 server you reach with your normal `ssh`, `scp` and `sftp` clients — implemented in pure JavaScript\n([`ssh.js`](ssh.js), [`sftp.js`](sftp.js)) and run **inside Vetro's Node process**. It ships no binary, because a\nSamsung TV refuses to execute unsigned native code (UEP); interpreted JS loaded by Vetro's already-signed Node is the\nway to run a server here. **Needs Node 10+ on the TV** (Ed25519 / ECDH); the 2021+ Tizen TVs that run Vetro's agent\nqualify. On older Node the Shard loads but reports \"unsupported\".\n\n## What you get, and why\n\nVetro's service runs as **uid 5001** (`owner`) under the Smack label `User::Pkg::vetrotvapp`, which has **no execute\naccess to system binaries** (`/bin/bash`, `/usr/bin/script` are floor-labeled). So this process cannot spawn a shell or\na PTY — it can only run things as root through Vetro's **agent** (`ctx.execute`), which is one command at a time.\n\n| Command | Runs as | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `ssh -p 2222 root@TV-IP` | **root** | interactive **line-shell**: each command you type runs via the agent, `cd` is remembered. **No PTY** — no `top`/`vi`/`less` (use `top -b -n1`), no shell state beyond `cwd` |\n| `ssh -p 2222 root@TV-IP '<command>'` | **root** | the command runs through the agent and returns its output (one-shot, ~60 s cap) |\n| `scp` / `sftp -P 2222` | **owner (uid 5001)** | file transfer, in-process; reaches owner-readable files |\n\nThe username is ignored — you authenticate with your key. The interactive shell and single commands run as **root**;\nfile transfer runs as the **owner**.\n\n> **Why no interactive root shell with a real terminal?** A PTY needs to spawn a shell process, which the sandbox\n> blocks, and the agent runs one command at a time (it can't stream a live terminal without holding Vetro's command\n> queue open). So the interactive shell is line-based: you type a command, it runs, you get the output. For anything\n> that needs a real terminal, there isn't a way on this platform today.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Generate a key if you don't have one: `ssh-keygen -t ed25519`.\n2. Open the Shard's page, paste your **public** key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub`) under *Authorized keys*, Save.\n3. Switch the Shard **on**. Connect: `ssh -p 2222 root@TV-IP`.\n\nKeys and the host key are stored in the Shard's own config, not in `~/.ssh` (root's home is read-only on the TV).\n\n## Algorithms\n\nOne of each, all accepted by a stock OpenSSH client and available on Node 12:\n\n- key exchange `ecdh-sha2-nistp256` · host key `ssh-ed25519` · cipher `aes256-ctr` · MAC `hmac-sha2-256`\n- user authentication: `publickey`, **ed25519 keys only** (v1)\n\nNo post-quantum KEX, so recent OpenSSH prints a \"not using a post-quantum key exchange\" notice — expected. The server\n**refuses the PTY request** on purpose, so your client prints \"PTY allocation request failed\" and drops to line mode —\nthat is the line-shell working as intended.\n\n## Commands it runs\n\n`exec` permission is used to run, through `ctx.execute` (as root via Vetro's agent), the commands you send over SSH —\n**nothing runs unless you type it**. SFTP does **not** use the agent; it runs in Vetro's own process as uid 5001.\n\n| Source | What runs | As |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| interactive shell | each line you type, wrapped as `cd '<cwd>'; <your line>; printf <marker><pwd>` so the directory carries over, via `ctx.execute` | root (agent) |\n| a command over SSH | the command you typed, verbatim, via `ctx.execute` | root (agent) |\n| `scp`/`sftp` | Node `fs` operations (open/read/write/readdir/…) | uid 5001, in-process |\n\n## Network\n\nIt opens no outbound connection and downloads nothing. The only listener is this SSH server, on the port you set\n(default 2222), bound to **all interfaces** (`0.0.0.0`) — so it is reachable from anywhere that can route to the TV.\nVetro's traffic is plain HTTP — keep the TV on a trusted network and **never expose the SSH port to the Internet**.\n\n## Data it keeps\n\nIn the Shard's config (`config.json`): the port, your authorized public keys, and the generated Ed25519 **host key**\n(so your client doesn't warn about a changed key after a restart). Removing the Shard deletes all of it. *Regenerate\nhost key* on the page makes a new one (clients that connected before will warn once).\n\n## Security note\n\nThis is a hand-written SSH server guarding a root command path on your TV. It has been exercised against OpenSSH\n`ssh`/`scp`/`sftp` but has **not** had a third-party security review. Every async path is wrapped so a fault cannot\ncrash the Vetro service. Pre-auth abuse is bounded: a 30 s login grace period, at most 8 half-open (unauthenticated)\nconnections, and a few auth attempts per connection, so a host on the LAN can't tie up Vetro's memory with half-open\nsessions. Switching the Shard off (or Vetro disabling it) tears down every live connection, including open SFTP\nsessions. Run it on a trusted LAN, key auth only (there is no password auth), and read [`ssh.js`](ssh.js) before you\ntrust it. Not affiliated with OpenSSH or dropbear.\n\n## Tested\n\n_On the TV — Samsung The Frame **QN75LS03B** (2022, `22_PONTUSM_FTV`), Tizen 6.5.0, kernel 5.4.77 `armv7l`, Vetro 0.5.0_\n(installed through Vetro's plugin host in Developer mode, trust `file`), with an OpenSSH 10.3 client over the LAN:\n\n- `ssh root@tv '<cmd>'` runs as **root** (`id` → `uid=0(root)`); the command's **exit status is forwarded**\n  (`exit 7` → 7, `exit 42` → 42, `true` → 0);\n- the interactive **line-shell** works and remembers `cwd` (`pwd` → `/`, `cd /tmp`, `pwd` → `/tmp`), no PTY as designed;\n- **`sftp` get + put of a 3 MB file is byte-identical** (same SHA-256) — this exercises the `CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST`\n  fix, since an upload past the initial ~2 MB window used to stall;\n- the plugin stayed healthy throughout (host reports `errors: 0`, `lastError: null`); installing and exercising it did\n  **not** crash the Vetro service.\n\nThe diagnosis above (Smack label `User::Pkg::vetrotvapp` has no execute access to system binaries) is from this TV.\n\n_Off-device (OpenSSH 10.3 client, server on Node 22):_ key-exchange, ed25519 auth, the line-shell, `ssh root@tv 'cmd'`,\n`sftp`/`scp` get+put of a 6 MB binary (byte-identical, upload past the old window stall), the pre-auth limits (login\ngrace, half-open cap, auth-attempt cap), a re-key request answered with a clean disconnect, and `stop()` tearing down a\nlive session — all with clean teardown.\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// SSH server (in-process, pure JS): a real SSH-2 endpoint you reach with your normal ssh/scp/sftp client, implemented\n// in JavaScript (ssh.js + sftp.js) and run inside Vetro's Node process. No binary, so it works on a Tizen TV that\n// refuses unsigned native code (UEP). See README.md for the design and its limits.\n//\n// Why the shell is \"line\" not \"PTY\": the Vetro service runs as uid 5001 under Smack label User::Pkg::vetrotvapp, which\n// has no execute access to system binaries (/bin/bash, /usr/bin/script are floor-labeled). So this process cannot spawn\n// a shell or a PTY at all. Root is reachable only as one-shot commands through Vetro's agent (ctx.execute). Therefore:\n//   * `ssh you@tv`              -> a ROOT line-shell: each command you type runs via the agent, cwd remembered, no PTY\n//                                  (no top/vi/less -- use `top -b -n1`), no shell state beyond cwd\n//   * `ssh root@tv '<command>'` -> the command runs as root through the agent (one-shot), output returned\n//   * `sftp` / `scp`            -> file transfer in-process as the owner (uid 5001); reaches owner-readable files\n//\n// Everything that could throw asynchronously is wrapped: a plugin crash would take down the whole Vetro service.\n\nvar crypto = require('crypto');\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\n\nvar DEFAULT_PORT = 2222;\nvar EXEC_TIMEOUT = 60000;          // Vetro's shared command queue caps a single root command\nvar EXIT = {};                     // sentinel queued to end a line-shell session\n\nfunction strBytes(s) { return Buffer.from && Buffer.from !== Uint8Array.from ? Buffer.from(s) : new Buffer(s); }\nfunction shQuote(s) { return \"'\" + String(s).replace(/'/g, \"'\\\\''\") + \"'\"; }\nfunction crlf(s) { return String(s).replace(/\\r?\\n/g, '\\r\\n'); }\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var server = null, logLines = [], page = null;\n    var fingerprint = null, unsupported = null, lastError = null, connections = 0;\n\n    function log(m) { logLines.push(new Date().toISOString().slice(11, 19) + ' ' + m); if (logLines.length > 120) logLines.shift(); }\n    function cfg() { try { var c = ctx.config.get(); return c && typeof c === 'object' && !Array.isArray(c) ? c : {}; } catch (e) { return {}; } }\n    function saveCfg(patch) { var c = cfg(); for (var k in patch) if (patch.hasOwnProperty(k)) c[k] = patch[k]; try { ctx.config.set(c); return true; } catch (e) { log('config not saved: ' + e.message); return false; } }\n    function port() { var p = cfg().port; return (typeof p === 'number' && p >= 1 && p <= 65535 && p % 1 === 0) ? p : DEFAULT_PORT; }\n    function authText() { var a = cfg().authorizedKeys; return typeof a === 'string' ? a : ''; }\n    function countKeys(text) { var n = 0; String(text || '').split('\\n').forEach(function (l) { if (/^ssh-ed25519\\s/.test(l.trim())) n++; }); return n; }\n\n    // Run one command as root through Vetro's agent, carrying the working directory across commands (same idea as the\n    // Shell Shard): the command runs in `cwd`, and the directory it ends in comes back after a marker with a per-call\n    // nonce so a command's own output cannot fake it. cb(outputText, newCwd).\n    function runAgent(cwd, cmd, cb) {\n        var nonce = crypto.randomBytes(8).toString('hex'), marker = '__VCWD_' + nonce + '__';\n        var script = 'cd ' + shQuote(cwd) + ' 2>/dev/null || cd /\\n' + cmd + '\\n__vs=$?\\nprintf \"\\\\n' + marker + '%s\\\\n\" \"$(pwd)\" 2>/dev/null\\nexit $__vs\\n';\n        var b64 = strBytes(script).toString('base64');\n        // Decode the script into a variable and run it with -c, so the command's own stdin can be /dev/null (a command\n        // that waits for input ends instead of holding Vetro's command queue). Piping the script to `sh </dev/null`\n        // would feed sh an empty script.\n        var wrapped = '__vscript=\"$(printf %s ' + b64 + ' | base64 -d)\"; if command -v bash >/dev/null 2>&1; then exec bash -c \"$__vscript\" </dev/null; else exec sh -c \"$__vscript\" </dev/null; fi';\n        var done = false;\n        function finish(out, ncwd, code) { if (done) return; done = true; try { cb(out, ncwd, code); } catch (e) { log('shell cb error: ' + e.message); } }\n        var p;\n        try { p = ctx.execute(wrapped, EXEC_TIMEOUT); } catch (e) { return finish('vetro: ' + e.message + '\\n', cwd, 255); }\n        p.then(function (r) {\n            try {\n                var out = String((r && r.stdout) || ''), mark = '\\n' + marker, i = out.lastIndexOf(mark), ncwd = cwd;\n                if (i >= 0) { var rest = out.slice(i + mark.length), nl = rest.indexOf('\\n'), found = nl < 0 ? rest : rest.slice(0, nl); if (found.charAt(0) === '/') ncwd = found; out = out.slice(0, i); }\n                if (r && r.stderr) out += String(r.stderr);\n                var code = (r && typeof r.exit_code === 'number') ? r.exit_code : 0;\n                if (r && r.timed_out) { out += '\\n[stopped after ' + (EXEC_TIMEOUT / 1000) + ' s: time limit]\\n'; code = 124; }\n                finish(out, ncwd, code);\n            } catch (e) { finish('vetro: ' + e.message + '\\n', cwd, 255); }\n        }, function (e) { finish('vetro: ' + (e && e.message || e) + '\\n', cwd, 255); });\n    }\n\n    // Interactive ROOT line-shell on a channel with no PTY (we refuse pty-req, so the client is line-buffered with local\n    // echo). We send output and prompts only; we never echo input.\n    function rootLineShell(ch) {\n        var cwd = '/', buf = '', busy = false, queue = [], closed = false, eofSeen = false;\n        function prompt() { return 'root@tv:' + cwd + '# '; }\n        function endSession() { if (closed) return; closed = true; try { ch.exit(0); } catch (e) {} }\n        try {\n            ch.write('Vetro root shell — each command runs as root via Vetro\\'s agent.\\r\\n');\n            ch.write('No PTY: full-screen programs (top, vi, less) will not work; use e.g. `top -b -n1`. `exit` to quit.\\r\\n');\n            ch.write(prompt());\n        } catch (e) {}\n        function pump() {\n            if (busy || closed) return;\n            if (!queue.length) { if (eofSeen) endSession(); return; }   // drain the queue before honoring EOF\n            var line = queue.shift();\n            if (line === EXIT) { try { ch.write('bye\\r\\n'); } catch (e) {} return endSession(); }\n            if (line === '') { try { ch.write(prompt()); } catch (e) {} return pump(); }\n            busy = true;\n            runAgent(cwd, line, function (out, ncwd) {\n                cwd = ncwd;\n                try { if (out) ch.write(crlf(out)); ch.write(prompt()); } catch (e) {}\n                busy = false; pump();\n            });\n        }\n        ch.on('data', function (d) {\n            try {\n                buf += d.toString('utf8');\n                var m;\n                while ((m = /\\r\\n|\\n|\\r/.exec(buf))) {\n                    var line = buf.slice(0, m.index); buf = buf.slice(m.index + m[0].length);\n                    line = line.replace(/\\x03/g, '');            // drop ^C bytes\n                    var t = line.replace(/^\\s+|\\s+$/g, '');\n                    if (t === 'exit' || t === 'logout') queue.push(EXIT);\n                    else if (t === '') queue.push('');\n                    else queue.push(line);\n                }\n                if (buf.length > 1 << 20) buf = '';               // runaway line without newline: drop it\n                pump();\n            } catch (e) { try { ch.write('shell error: ' + e.message + '\\r\\n'); } catch (x) {} }\n        });\n        ch.on('eof', function () { eofSeen = true; pump(); });   // exit once the queue has drained\n        ch.on('close', function () { closed = true; });\n    }\n\n    // `ssh ... '<command>'` -> one-shot root command (output returned, then the channel closes). The command's real\n    // exit status is forwarded, so `ssh tv 'cmd' && ...` works in scripts.\n    function runExec(ch, cmd) {\n        runAgent('/', cmd, function (out, ncwd, code) {\n            try { if (out) ch.write(out); ch.exit(typeof code === 'number' ? code : 0); } catch (e) {}\n        });\n    }\n\n    function wire(ssh, sftp) {\n        server.on('connection', function (conn) { connections++; log('client connected'); conn.on('end', function () { if (connections > 0) connections--; }); });\n        server.on('shell', function (ch) { try { rootLineShell(ch); } catch (e) { log('shell error: ' + e.message); try { ch.exit(1); } catch (x) {} } });\n        server.on('exec', function (ch, cmd) { log('root one-shot command (' + String(cmd).length + ' chars)'); try { runExec(ch, cmd); } catch (e) { try { ch.exit(1); } catch (x) {} } });\n        server.on('subsystem', function (ch, name) { try { if (name === 'sftp') sftp.serve(ch, { log: log }); else ch.close(); } catch (e) { log('sftp error: ' + e.message); try { ch.close(); } catch (x) {} } });\n    }\n\n    function startServer() {\n        var ssh, sftp;\n        try { ssh = require('./ssh.js'); sftp = require('./sftp.js'); }\n        catch (e) { unsupported = 'This TV\\'s Node is too old for the SSH module (needs Node 10+): ' + e.message; log(unsupported); return; }\n        try {\n            var c = cfg();\n            server = ssh.createServer({ hostKeyPem: c.hostKeyPem, authorizedKeys: authText(), allowPty: false, log: log });\n            if (!c.hostKeyPem) saveCfg({ hostKeyPem: server.hostKeyPem() });\n            fingerprint = 'SHA256:' + crypto.createHash('sha256').update(server.hostKey.blob).digest('base64').replace(/=+$/, '');\n            wire(ssh, sftp);\n            server.listen(port(), '0.0.0.0', function () { lastError = null; log('listening on 0.0.0.0:' + port()); });\n        } catch (e) { unsupported = 'Could not start the SSH server: ' + e.message; lastError = e.message; log(unsupported); server = null; }\n    }\n    function stopServer() { if (server) { try { server.close(); } catch (e) {} server = null; } connections = 0; }\n\n    function loadPage() {\n        var places = [path.join(__dirname, 'ui.html'), path.join(ctx.dir || '', 'ui.html')];\n        for (var i = 0; i < places.length; i++) { try { return fs.readFileSync(places[i], 'utf8'); } catch (e) {} }\n        return '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p>Page file missing: reinstall this Shard.</p>';\n    }\n    function json(res, body, code) { res.writeHead(code || 200, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' }); res.end(JSON.stringify(body)); }\n    function readJson(req, cb) {\n        var chunks = [], size = 0, done = false;\n        req.on('data', function (c) { size += c.length; if (size > 65536) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(new Error('Request too large')); } req.destroy && req.destroy(); return; } chunks.push(c); });\n        req.on('end', function () { if (done) return; done = true; var p; try { p = JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8') || '{}'); } catch (e) { return cb(new Error('Invalid JSON')); } if (!p || typeof p !== 'object' || Array.isArray(p)) return cb(new Error('Invalid JSON')); cb(null, p); });\n        req.on('error', function (e) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(e); } });\n    }\n    function state() {\n        return { running: !!(server && server.listening), port: port(), fingerprint: fingerprint, unsupported: unsupported,\n            lastError: (server && server.lastError) || lastError, connections: connections, keyCount: countKeys(authText()), log: logLines };\n    }\n\n    return {\n        start: function () { page = loadPage(); unsupported = null; lastError = null; try { startServer(); } catch (e) { log('start error: ' + e.message); } },\n        stop: function () { try { stopServer(); } catch (e) {} page = null; },\n        status: function () { return { running: !!(server && server.listening), port: port(), connections: connections, unsupported: unsupported ? true : undefined }; },\n\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') { res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' }); res.end(page || loadPage()); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'state' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, state()); return true; }\n            if (req.method !== 'POST') return false;\n\n            if (sub === 'authkeys') {\n                readJson(req, function (err, p) {\n                    if (err) return json(res, { ok: false, error: err.message }, 400);\n                    var keys = typeof p.keys === 'string' ? p.keys : '';\n                    if (keys.length > 16384) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'authorized_keys too large' }, 400);\n                    if (/\\S/.test(keys) && !/^ssh-ed25519\\s/m.test(keys)) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'Only ssh-ed25519 public keys are supported in v1' }, 400);\n                    saveCfg({ authorizedKeys: keys });\n                    if (server) server.setAuthorizedKeys(keys);\n                    log('authorized_keys updated (' + countKeys(keys) + ' key(s))');\n                    json(res, state());\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'port') {\n                readJson(req, function (err, p) {\n                    if (err) return json(res, { ok: false, error: err.message }, 400);\n                    if (typeof p.port !== 'number' || p.port < 1 || p.port > 65535 || p.port % 1 !== 0) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'port must be 1-65535' }, 400);\n                    saveCfg({ port: p.port });\n                    if (server) { stopServer(); startServer(); }\n                    json(res, state());\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'regen-hostkey') {\n                saveCfg({ hostKeyPem: null });\n                if (server) { stopServer(); startServer(); }\n                log('host key regenerated');\n                json(res, state());\n                return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\n","sftp.js":"'use strict';\n// SFTP version 3 server over one SSH channel, backed by Node's fs. This is what makes `scp` (modern OpenSSH uses\n// SFTP under the hood) and `sftp` work against this server — no sftp-server binary needed on the TV. ES5 syntax,\n// async fs so a big transfer does not block Vetro's single process. draft-ietf-secsh-filexfer-02.\n\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\n\nvar T = { INIT: 1, VERSION: 2, OPEN: 3, CLOSE: 4, READ: 5, WRITE: 6, LSTAT: 7, FSTAT: 8, SETSTAT: 9, FSETSTAT: 10,\n    OPENDIR: 11, READDIR: 12, REMOVE: 13, MKDIR: 14, RMDIR: 15, REALPATH: 16, STAT: 17, RENAME: 18, READLINK: 19, SYMLINK: 20,\n    STATUS: 101, HANDLE: 102, DATA: 103, NAME: 104, ATTRS: 105 };\nvar FX = { OK: 0, EOF: 1, NO_SUCH_FILE: 2, PERMISSION_DENIED: 3, FAILURE: 4, OP_UNSUPPORTED: 8 };\nvar F = { READ: 0x01, WRITE: 0x02, APPEND: 0x04, CREAT: 0x08, TRUNC: 0x10, EXCL: 0x20 };\nvar A = { SIZE: 0x01, UIDGID: 0x02, PERMISSIONS: 0x04, ACMODTIME: 0x08 };\n\nfunction errStatus(e) {\n    if (!e) return FX.FAILURE;\n    if (e.code === 'ENOENT') return FX.NO_SUCH_FILE;\n    if (e.code === 'EACCES' || e.code === 'EPERM') return FX.PERMISSION_DENIED;\n    return FX.FAILURE;\n}\n\n// ---- tiny writer (length-prefixed SFTP packet) ----\nfunction Pkt(type) { this.parts = []; this.type = type; }\nPkt.prototype.u32 = function (n) { var b = Buffer.alloc(4); b.writeUInt32BE(n >>> 0, 0); this.parts.push(b); return this; };\nPkt.prototype.u64 = function (n) { var b = Buffer.alloc(8); var hi = Math.floor(n / 4294967296); b.writeUInt32BE(hi >>> 0, 0); b.writeUInt32BE((n >>> 0), 4); this.parts.push(b); return this; };\nPkt.prototype.byte = function (n) { this.parts.push(Buffer.from([n & 0xff])); return this; };\nPkt.prototype.str = function (s) { if (typeof s === 'string') s = Buffer.from(s, 'utf8'); var l = Buffer.alloc(4); l.writeUInt32BE(s.length, 0); this.parts.push(l, s); return this; };\nPkt.prototype.raw = function (b) { this.parts.push(b); return this; };\nPkt.prototype.done = function () {\n    var body = Buffer.concat(this.parts), head = Buffer.alloc(5);\n    head.writeUInt32BE(body.length + 1, 0); head[4] = this.type;\n    return Buffer.concat([head, body]);\n};\n\nfunction Reader(buf) { this.b = buf; this.p = 0; }\nReader.prototype.u32 = function () { var n = this.b.readUInt32BE(this.p); this.p += 4; return n; };\nReader.prototype.u64 = function () { var hi = this.b.readUInt32BE(this.p), lo = this.b.readUInt32BE(this.p + 4); this.p += 8; return hi * 4294967296 + lo; };\nReader.prototype.byte = function () { return this.b[this.p++]; };\nReader.prototype.str = function () { var l = this.u32(); var s = this.b.slice(this.p, this.p + l); this.p += l; return s; };\n\nfunction attrsBuf(st) {\n    var p = new Pkt(0); // reuse as plain writer; type unused here\n    var flags = A.SIZE | A.UIDGID | A.PERMISSIONS | A.ACMODTIME;\n    var w = [];\n    var b = Buffer.alloc(4); b.writeUInt32BE(flags, 0); w.push(b);\n    var sz = Buffer.alloc(8); var hi = Math.floor(st.size / 4294967296); sz.writeUInt32BE(hi >>> 0, 0); sz.writeUInt32BE((st.size >>> 0), 4); w.push(sz);\n    var ug = Buffer.alloc(8); ug.writeUInt32BE(st.uid >>> 0, 0); ug.writeUInt32BE(st.gid >>> 0, 4); w.push(ug);\n    var pm = Buffer.alloc(4); pm.writeUInt32BE(st.mode >>> 0, 0); w.push(pm);\n    var tm = Buffer.alloc(8); tm.writeUInt32BE(Math.floor(st.atimeMs / 1000) >>> 0, 0); tm.writeUInt32BE(Math.floor(st.mtimeMs / 1000) >>> 0, 4); w.push(tm);\n    return Buffer.concat(w);\n}\nfunction skipAttrs(r) {\n    var flags = r.u32(), out = {};\n    if (flags & A.SIZE) out.size = r.u64();\n    if (flags & A.UIDGID) { out.uid = r.u32(); out.gid = r.u32(); }\n    if (flags & A.PERMISSIONS) out.mode = r.u32();\n    if (flags & A.ACMODTIME) { out.atime = r.u32(); out.mtime = r.u32(); }\n    return out;\n}\n\nfunction modeString(st) {\n    var m = st.mode, t = '-';\n    if (st.isDirectory()) t = 'd'; else if (st.isSymbolicLink()) t = 'l'; else if (st.isCharacterDevice()) t = 'c'; else if (st.isBlockDevice()) t = 'b'; else if (st.isFIFO()) t = 'p'; else if (st.isSocket()) t = 's';\n    var rwx = ['---', '--x', '-w-', '-wx', 'r--', 'r-x', 'rw-', 'rwx'];\n    return t + rwx[(m >> 6) & 7] + rwx[(m >> 3) & 7] + rwx[m & 7];\n}\nfunction longname(name, st) {\n    var d = new Date(st.mtimeMs), mon = ['Jan','Feb','Mar','Apr','May','Jun','Jul','Aug','Sep','Oct','Nov','Dec'][d.getMonth()];\n    var day = ('  ' + d.getDate()).slice(-2), hm = ('0' + d.getHours()).slice(-2) + ':' + ('0' + d.getMinutes()).slice(-2);\n    var size = ('           ' + st.size).slice(-11);\n    return modeString(st) + ' 1 ' + ('     ' + (st.uid >>> 0)).slice(-5) + ' ' + ('     ' + (st.gid >>> 0)).slice(-5) + ' ' + size + ' ' + mon + ' ' + day + ' ' + hm + ' ' + name;\n}\n\n// Attach an SFTP server to a channel. opts: { log }\nfunction serve(channel, opts) {\n    opts = opts || {}; var log = opts.log || function () {};\n    var inbuf = Buffer.alloc(0);\n    var handles = {}, nextH = 0;\n\n    function reply(buf) { channel.write(buf); }\n    function status(id, code, msg) { reply(new Pkt(T.STATUS).u32(id).u32(code).str(msg || '').str('').done()); }\n    function newHandle(obj) { var h = 'h' + (nextH++); handles[h] = obj; return h; }\n    // Wrap an async fs callback so a throw inside it (e.g. building the reply) is caught and logged instead of\n    // escaping uncaught — an uncaught throw in a callback would take down the whole Vetro process. The sync dispatch\n    // in process() is already guarded, but that try does not cover these callbacks.\n    function safe(fn) { return function () { try { return fn.apply(this, arguments); } catch (e) { if (opts.log) opts.log('sftp cb error: ' + (e && e.message || e)); } }; }\n\n    channel.on('data', function (d) { inbuf = Buffer.concat([inbuf, d]); process(); });\n    // The sftp client signals it is done by sending CHANNEL_EOF and then waits for the server to close the channel.\n    // Release handles and finish the channel (exit-status + eof + close) so the client can disconnect.\n    channel.on('eof', function () { closeAll(); if (channel.exit) channel.exit(0); });\n    channel.on('close', function () { closeAll(); });\n\n    function closeAll() {\n        for (var h in handles) { if (handles[h] && handles[h].fd != null) { try { fs.close(handles[h].fd, function () {}); } catch (e) {} } }\n        handles = {};\n    }\n\n    function process() {\n        while (inbuf.length >= 4) {\n            var len = inbuf.readUInt32BE(0);\n            if (len > 256 * 1024 + 64) { channel.close(); return; }      // oversized frame: bail\n            if (inbuf.length < 4 + len) return;\n            var frame = inbuf.slice(4, 4 + len); inbuf = inbuf.slice(4 + len);\n            try { handle(frame[0], new Reader(frame.slice(1))); } catch (e) { if (opts.log) opts.log('sftp handler error: ' + (e && e.message || e)); }\n        }\n    }\n\n    function handle(type, r) {\n        if (type === T.INIT) { r.u32(); return reply(new Pkt(T.VERSION).u32(3).done()); }\n        var id = r.u32();\n        switch (type) {\n            case T.REALPATH: {\n                var p = r.str().toString('utf8') || '.';\n                var abs = path.resolve(p);\n                return reply(new Pkt(T.NAME).u32(id).u32(1).str(abs).str(abs).raw(Buffer.alloc(4)).done()); // one name, empty attrs\n            }\n            case T.STAT: case T.LSTAT: {\n                var sp = r.str().toString('utf8'); var fn = type === T.STAT ? fs.stat : fs.lstat;\n                return fn(sp, safe(function (e, st) { if (e) return status(id, errStatus(e), e.message); reply(new Pkt(T.ATTRS).u32(id).raw(attrsBuf(st)).done()); }));\n            }\n            case T.FSTAT: {\n                var hd = handles[r.str().toString()]; if (!hd || hd.fd == null) return status(id, FX.FAILURE, 'bad handle');\n                return fs.fstat(hd.fd, safe(function (e, st) { if (e) return status(id, errStatus(e), e.message); reply(new Pkt(T.ATTRS).u32(id).raw(attrsBuf(st)).done()); }));\n            }\n            case T.OPEN: {\n                var fp = r.str().toString('utf8'); var pf = r.u32(); skipAttrs(r);\n                var flags = (pf & F.WRITE) ? ((pf & F.READ) ? 'r+' : 'w') : 'r';\n                if (pf & F.APPEND) flags = 'a';\n                if ((pf & F.CREAT) && (pf & F.EXCL)) flags = 'wx';\n                else if ((pf & F.CREAT) && (pf & F.TRUNC)) flags = 'w';\n                else if ((pf & F.CREAT) && (pf & F.WRITE)) flags = (pf & F.READ) ? 'a+' : 'a';\n                if ((pf & F.WRITE) && (pf & F.TRUNC)) flags = (pf & F.READ) ? 'w+' : 'w';\n                return fs.open(fp, flags, safe(function (e, fd) {\n                    if (e) return status(id, errStatus(e), e.message);\n                    reply(new Pkt(T.HANDLE).u32(id).str(newHandle({ fd: fd, path: fp })).done());\n                }));\n            }\n            case T.READ: {\n                var rh = handles[r.str().toString()]; var off = r.u64(), rl = r.u32();\n                if (!rh || rh.fd == null) return status(id, FX.FAILURE, 'bad handle');\n                var buf = Buffer.alloc(Math.min(rl, 256 * 1024));\n                return fs.read(rh.fd, buf, 0, buf.length, off, safe(function (e, n) {\n                    if (e) return status(id, errStatus(e), e.message);\n                    if (n === 0) return status(id, FX.EOF);\n                    reply(new Pkt(T.DATA).u32(id).str(buf.slice(0, n)).done());\n                }));\n            }\n            case T.WRITE: {\n                var wh = handles[r.str().toString()]; var woff = r.u64(), wdata = r.str();\n                if (!wh || wh.fd == null) return status(id, FX.FAILURE, 'bad handle');\n                return fs.write(wh.fd, wdata, 0, wdata.length, woff, safe(function (e) { status(id, e ? errStatus(e) : FX.OK, e ? e.message : ''); }));\n            }\n            case T.CLOSE: {\n                var hk = r.str().toString(), ch = handles[hk]; delete handles[hk];\n                if (ch && ch.fd != null) return fs.close(ch.fd, safe(function (e) { status(id, e ? errStatus(e) : FX.OK, e ? e.message : ''); }));\n                return status(id, FX.OK);\n            }\n            case T.OPENDIR: {\n                var dp = r.str().toString('utf8');\n                return fs.readdir(dp, safe(function (e, names) { if (e) return status(id, errStatus(e), e.message); reply(new Pkt(T.HANDLE).u32(id).str(newHandle({ dir: dp, names: names, i: 0 })).done()); }));\n            }\n            case T.READDIR: {\n                var dh = handles[r.str().toString()]; if (!dh || !dh.names) return status(id, FX.FAILURE, 'bad handle');\n                if (dh.i >= dh.names.length) return status(id, FX.EOF);\n                var batch = dh.names.slice(dh.i, dh.i + 64); dh.i += batch.length;\n                var entries = [], pending = batch.length;\n                if (!pending) return status(id, FX.EOF);\n                batch.forEach(function (nm) {\n                    fs.lstat(path.join(dh.dir, nm), safe(function (e, st) {\n                        entries.push({ name: nm, st: e ? null : st });\n                        if (--pending === 0) {\n                            var pkt = new Pkt(T.NAME).u32(id).u32(entries.length);\n                            entries.forEach(function (en) {\n                                var st2 = en.st || { size: 0, uid: 0, gid: 0, mode: 0, atimeMs: 0, mtimeMs: 0, isDirectory: function () { return false; }, isSymbolicLink: function () { return false; }, isCharacterDevice: function () { return false; }, isBlockDevice: function () { return false; }, isFIFO: function () { return false; }, isSocket: function () { return false; } };\n                                pkt.str(en.name).str(longname(en.name, st2)).raw(attrsBuf(st2));\n                            });\n                            reply(pkt.done());\n                        }\n                    }));\n                });\n                return;\n            }\n            case T.REMOVE: { var rp = r.str().toString('utf8'); return fs.unlink(rp, safe(function (e) { status(id, e ? errStatus(e) : FX.OK, e ? e.message : ''); })); }\n            case T.MKDIR: { var mp = r.str().toString('utf8'); skipAttrs(r); return fs.mkdir(mp, safe(function (e) { status(id, e ? errStatus(e) : FX.OK, e ? e.message : ''); })); }\n            case T.RMDIR: { var rmp = r.str().toString('utf8'); return fs.rmdir(rmp, safe(function (e) { status(id, e ? errStatus(e) : FX.OK, e ? e.message : ''); })); }\n            case T.RENAME: { var op = r.str().toString('utf8'), np = r.str().toString('utf8'); return fs.rename(op, np, safe(function (e) { status(id, e ? errStatus(e) : FX.OK, e ? e.message : ''); })); }\n            case T.SETSTAT: case T.FSETSTAT: {\n                var target, isH = type === T.FSETSTAT;\n                if (isH) { var sh = handles[r.str().toString()]; target = sh && sh.path; } else target = r.str().toString('utf8');\n                var at = skipAttrs(r);\n                if (!target) return status(id, FX.OK);\n                var steps = [];\n                if (at.mode != null) steps.push(function (cb) { fs.chmod(target, at.mode & 0xfff, cb); });\n                if (at.size != null) steps.push(function (cb) { fs.truncate(target, at.size, cb); });\n                if (at.atime != null && at.mtime != null) steps.push(function (cb) { fs.utimes(target, at.atime, at.mtime, cb); });\n                (function run(i) { if (i >= steps.length) return status(id, FX.OK); steps[i](safe(function (e) { if (e) return status(id, errStatus(e), e.message); run(i + 1); })); })(0);\n                return;\n            }\n            case T.READLINK: { var lp = r.str().toString('utf8'); return fs.readlink(lp, safe(function (e, t) { if (e) return status(id, errStatus(e), e.message); reply(new Pkt(T.NAME).u32(id).u32(1).str(t).str(t).raw(Buffer.alloc(4)).done()); })); }\n            default: return status(id, FX.OP_UNSUPPORTED, 'unsupported');\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { serve: serve };\n","ssh.js":"'use strict';\n// A small SSH-2 server in pure JavaScript, leaning on Node's crypto for the maths. No native code and no npm\n// dependencies, so it runs as unsigned JS inside Vetro's already-signed Node process (the only way to run code on a\n// signature-enforced Tizen TV). It needs Node 10+ (Ed25519, createECDH) — the TV this targets runs Node 12.\n//\n// Algorithms (one of each, all supported by a stock OpenSSH client and available on Node 12):\n//   kex      ecdh-sha2-nistp256        (crypto.createECDH('prime256v1'))\n//   hostkey  ssh-ed25519               (crypto.sign(null, H, key))\n//   cipher   aes256-ctr                (both directions)\n//   mac      hmac-sha2-256             (encrypt-and-mac, mac over seq||plaintext)\n//   userauth publickey, ssh-ed25519 keys only\n//\n// Written in ES5 syntax (var/function) so it still packs through the catalog's ES5 check, even though it only RUNS on\n// a modern-Node TV. Security-sensitive: read it before trusting it with a root login. RFCs 4251-4254, 5656.\n\nvar crypto = require('crypto');\nvar net = require('net');\nvar EventEmitter = require('events').EventEmitter;\n\n// ---- message numbers ----\nvar MSG = {\n    DISCONNECT: 1, IGNORE: 2, UNIMPLEMENTED: 3, DEBUG: 4, SERVICE_REQUEST: 5, SERVICE_ACCEPT: 6, EXT_INFO: 7,\n    KEXINIT: 20, NEWKEYS: 21, KEX_ECDH_INIT: 30, KEX_ECDH_REPLY: 31,\n    USERAUTH_REQUEST: 50, USERAUTH_FAILURE: 51, USERAUTH_SUCCESS: 52, USERAUTH_BANNER: 53, USERAUTH_PK_OK: 60,\n    GLOBAL_REQUEST: 80, REQUEST_SUCCESS: 81, REQUEST_FAILURE: 82,\n    CHANNEL_OPEN: 90, CHANNEL_OPEN_CONFIRMATION: 91, CHANNEL_OPEN_FAILURE: 92, CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST: 93,\n    CHANNEL_DATA: 94, CHANNEL_EXTENDED_DATA: 95, CHANNEL_EOF: 96, CHANNEL_CLOSE: 97,\n    CHANNEL_REQUEST: 98, CHANNEL_SUCCESS: 99, CHANNEL_FAILURE: 100\n};\nvar SERVER_ID = 'SSH-2.0-VetroSSH_0.1';\n\n// ---- buffer writer / reader (SSH wire types) ----\nfunction Writer() { this.parts = []; }\nWriter.prototype.byte = function (n) { var b = Buffer.alloc(1); b[0] = n & 0xff; this.parts.push(b); return this; };\nWriter.prototype.bool = function (v) { return this.byte(v ? 1 : 0); };\nWriter.prototype.u32 = function (n) { var b = Buffer.alloc(4); b.writeUInt32BE(n >>> 0, 0); this.parts.push(b); return this; };\nWriter.prototype.raw = function (buf) { this.parts.push(buf); return this; };\nWriter.prototype.string = function (buf) { if (typeof buf === 'string') buf = Buffer.from(buf, 'utf8'); var l = Buffer.alloc(4); l.writeUInt32BE(buf.length, 0); this.parts.push(l, buf); return this; };\nWriter.prototype.mpint = function (buf) {\n    // positive multi-precision integer: drop leading zero bytes, prepend 0x00 if the high bit is set.\n    var i = 0; while (i < buf.length - 1 && buf[i] === 0) i++;\n    buf = buf.slice(i);\n    if (buf.length && (buf[0] & 0x80)) buf = Buffer.concat([Buffer.from([0]), buf]);\n    return this.string(buf);\n};\nWriter.prototype.nameList = function (arr) { return this.string(arr.join(',')); };\nWriter.prototype.done = function () { return Buffer.concat(this.parts); };\n\nfunction Reader(buf) { this.buf = buf; this.pos = 0; }\nReader.prototype.byte = function () { return this.buf[this.pos++]; };\nReader.prototype.bool = function () { return this.buf[this.pos++] !== 0; };\nReader.prototype.u32 = function () { var n = this.buf.readUInt32BE(this.pos); this.pos += 4; return n; };\nReader.prototype.string = function () { var l = this.u32(); var s = this.buf.slice(this.pos, this.pos + l); this.pos += l; return s; };\nReader.prototype.rest = function () { return this.buf.slice(this.pos); };\n\nfunction sshString(buf) { return new Writer().string(buf).done(); }\n\n// ---- ed25519 host key: raw <-> KeyObject ----\nvar ED25519_SPKI_PREFIX = Buffer.from('302a300506032b6570032100', 'hex'); // DER prefix for a 32-byte Ed25519 public key\nfunction ed25519RawFromPublic(keyObject) { return keyObject.export({ type: 'spki', format: 'der' }).slice(-32); }\nfunction ed25519PublicFromRaw(raw) { return crypto.createPublicKey({ key: Buffer.concat([ED25519_SPKI_PREFIX, raw]), format: 'der', type: 'spki' }); }\nfunction hostKeyBlob(pubRaw) { return new Writer().string('ssh-ed25519').string(pubRaw).done(); }\n\n// Create (or load) a persistent Ed25519 host key. store = { get:fn, set:fn } of a PEM string; returns {priv, pubRaw, blob}.\nfunction loadHostKey(pem) {\n    var priv;\n    if (pem) { try { priv = crypto.createPrivateKey(pem); } catch (e) { priv = null; } }\n    var pubPem = null;\n    if (!priv) { var kp = crypto.generateKeyPairSync('ed25519'); priv = kp.privateKey; pubPem = kp.publicKey; }\n    var pub = pubPem || crypto.createPublicKey(priv);\n    var raw = ed25519RawFromPublic(pub);\n    return { priv: priv, pubRaw: raw, blob: hostKeyBlob(raw), pem: priv.export({ type: 'pkcs8', format: 'pem' }) };\n}\n\n// ---- authorized_keys: parse ssh-ed25519 entries into raw 32-byte keys ----\nfunction parseAuthorizedKeys(text) {\n    var out = [];\n    String(text || '').split('\\n').forEach(function (line) {\n        line = line.trim();\n        if (!line || line.charAt(0) === '#') return;\n        var parts = line.split(/\\s+/);\n        for (var i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {\n            if (parts[i] === 'ssh-ed25519' && parts[i + 1]) {\n                try {\n                    var blob = Buffer.from(parts[i + 1], 'base64');\n                    var r = new Reader(blob);\n                    if (r.string().toString() === 'ssh-ed25519') { var raw = r.string(); if (raw.length === 32) out.push(raw); }\n                } catch (e) { /* skip bad line */ }\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    });\n    return out;\n}\n\n// ================= per-connection state machine =================\nfunction Connection(socket, server) {\n    EventEmitter.call(this);\n    var self = this;\n    this.socket = socket;\n    this.server = server;\n    this.log = server.opts.log || function () {};\n    this.inbuf = Buffer.alloc(0);\n    this.gotId = false;\n    this.clientId = null;\n    this.seqIn = 0; this.seqOut = 0;\n    this.decipher = null; this.cipher = null; this.macInKey = null; this.macOutKey = null;\n    this.blockIn = 8; this.blockOut = 8; this.macInLen = 0; this.macOutLen = 0;\n    this.firstBlock = null;           // decrypted first block of the packet being read\n    this.sessionId = null;\n    this.authed = false; this.authUser = null;\n    this.channels = {};\n    this.nextChannelId = 0;\n    this.authTries = 0;\n    this.counted = true;                             // contributes to the server's half-open cap until authed or closed\n    server.pending = (server.pending || 0) + 1;\n\n    // Login grace timer: drop a connection that hasn't authenticated in time, so a peer can't sit half-open holding a\n    // packet buffer inside Vetro's process. Cleared on auth success and on cleanup.\n    var graceMs = (server.opts.loginGraceMs != null) ? server.opts.loginGraceMs : 30000;\n    if (graceMs > 0) this.graceTimer = setTimeout(function () {\n        if (self.authed || self._gone) return;\n        self.log('login grace time expired');\n        try { self.disconnect(2, 'login grace time expired'); } catch (e) {}\n        try { self.socket.destroy(); } catch (e) {}\n        self.cleanup();\n    }, graceMs);\n\n    socket.on('data', function (d) { try { self.onData(d); } catch (e) { self.fail(e); } });\n    socket.on('error', function (e) { self.log('socket error: ' + e.message); self.cleanup(); });\n    socket.on('close', function () { self.cleanup(); });\n\n    socket.write(SERVER_ID + '\\r\\n');\n}\nConnection.prototype = Object.create(EventEmitter.prototype);\n\nConnection.prototype.fail = function (e) { this.log('connection error: ' + (e && e.message || e)); try { this.socket.destroy(); } catch (x) {} this.cleanup(); };\nConnection.prototype.cleanup = function () {\n    if (this._gone) return; this._gone = true;\n    if (this.graceTimer) { clearTimeout(this.graceTimer); this.graceTimer = null; }\n    this._uncount();\n    for (var id in this.channels) if (this.channels[id]) this.channels[id]._shutdown();\n    this.emit('end');\n};\n// Release this connection's half-open slot exactly once (on auth success, or on close if never authed).\nConnection.prototype._uncount = function () { if (this.counted) { this.counted = false; if (this.server.pending > 0) this.server.pending--; } };\n\nConnection.prototype.onData = function (chunk) {\n    this.inbuf = Buffer.concat([this.inbuf, chunk]);\n    if (!this.gotId) {\n        var s = this.inbuf.indexOf('\\n');\n        if (s < 0) { if (this.inbuf.length > 4096) throw new Error('no ident'); return; }\n        var line = this.inbuf.slice(0, s).toString('binary').replace(/\\r$/, '');\n        if (line.slice(0, 4) !== 'SSH-') throw new Error('bad ident: ' + line);\n        this.clientId = line;\n        this.gotId = true;\n        this.inbuf = this.inbuf.slice(s + 1);\n    }\n    this.drain();\n};\n\